  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Rift volcanism: past, present and future</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Research and development activity contributing to the UK&#x2019;s strategy to address key development challenges.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Rift Volcanism project aims to improve the understanding of Rift Volcanism through three linked, multi-disciplinary work packages based on the past (What has driven eruptions over geological timescales?), present (What controls the active magmatic system and volcanic unrest?) and future (What are the potential threats from future volcanic activity?). The research focuses on the Main Ethiopian Rift area, and will primarily benefit Ethiopia via building institutional capacity in country to increase monitoring and decision-making capabilities, and knowledge sharing via volcanic activity monitoring organisations.</narrative>
  </description>
